SDL: FATAL — this program presents GPU frames from a blocking main loop.
             gucOS stops it before it takes the desktop down.

  program : blockyapp (pid 42) — webgpu.h surface
  detected: wgpuSurfacePresent() called from main(), not from a frame callback

  WHY: a blocking main loop never returns to the browser's event loop, so the
  browser can never recycle the GPU frames this program presents. That budget
  is finite. Exhausting it destroys the compositor's GPU device and the whole
  desktop goes black. gucOS refuses to start that countdown.

  FIX 1 — run it as-is, NO code changes:

      SDL_RENDER_DRIVER=software ./blockyapp

  Draws on the CPU into the window surface. There is no GPU frame budget, so a
  blocking loop is safe. Equivalent in code: SDL_CreateRenderer(win, "software").

  FIX 2 — keep GPU rendering, let SDL own the loop:

      #define SDL_MAIN_USE_CALLBACKS
      provide SDL_AppInit / SDL_AppIterate / SDL_AppEvent / SDL_AppQuit
      instead of your own while() loop.

  Standard SDL3 — the same source runs on desktop SDL3 unchanged.

  Details: /usr/share/doc/sdl-gucos.md

Exiting (status 69). The desktop is unaffected.

